   - `export function QuestsView({ quests, error, onRetry, onArrived }: { quests: QuestsResponse | null; error: string | null; onRetry: () => void; onArrived?: () => void }): ReactElement | null`. Move `QuestsPanel`'s error and loading blocks here verbatim, with Try again's `onClick={onRetry}`, then `return <QuestsList quests={quests} onArrived={onArrived} />;`.
   - `QuestsPanel` becomes `const { quests, error, reread } = useQuests(token); return <QuestsView quests={quests} error={error} onRetry={reread} />;`. Add a header line saying the landing (R2035000) shares this.

2. **`testids.ts`.** After `shop`, add `/** R2035000: the quests bookmark on the doors' box, its count and its parchment. */` followed by `questsBookmark: "landing-quests-bookmark"`, `questsCount: "landing-quests-count"` and `questsPanel: "landing-quests-panel"`.

3. **`landing.tsx`.** Imports: add `useCallback` and `useId` from react, `ECONOMY_LIVE` beside `GATE_SLOW_NOTICE_SECONDS`, `formatNumber` beside `t`, and `import { QuestsView, useQuests } from "./QuestsPanel.tsx";`. Add a header line: "R2035000 hangs the account's quests off the doors' box." Above `Actions`, add `QuestGlyph()`, which is `JlorePill.tsx`'s `Coin` (18px, class `landing-quests-glyph`) with the J path swapped for a `!`: `<path d="M12 6.5 V13.5" strokeWidth="2.2" strokeLinecap="round" …/>` and `<circle cx="12" cy="17.2" r="1.3" fill="currentColor" />`. Then add:
   ```tsx
   /** R2035000: how long the quests' parchment takes to unroll from its bookmark, and to roll back up. */
   export const QUESTS_UNROLL_MS = 220;

   type QuestsPhase = "closed" | "open" | "closing";

   /** R2035000: the account's quests behind a bookmark on the doors' box, read once on mount (CLAUDE.md rule 7). */
   function QuestsBookmark({ token, motion }: { token: string; motion: LandingMotion }): ReactElement | null {
     const { quests, error, reread } = useQuests(token);
     const [phase, setPhase] = useState<QuestsPhase>("closed");
     const root = useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null);
     const bookmark = useRef<HTMLButtonElement>(null);
     const panelId = useId();
     const close = useCallback((): void => {
       setPhase(motion === "reduced" ? "closed" : "closing");
     }, [motion]);

     // The roll back up ends hidden.
     useEffect(() => {
       if (phase !== "closing") return undefined;
       const timer = window.setTimeout(() => {
         setPhase("closed");
       }, QUESTS_UNROLL_MS);
       return () => {
         window.clearTimeout(timer);
       };
     }, [phase]);

     // While open: Escape closes it and gives the focus back; a press outside closes it.
     useEffect(() => {
       if (phase !== "open") return undefined;
       const onKey = (event: KeyboardEvent): void => {
         if (event.key !== "Escape") return;
         close();
         bookmark.current?.focus();
       };
       const onPress = (event: Event): void => {
         if (event.target instanceof Node && root.current?.contains(event.target) === true) return;
         close();
       };
       document.addEventListener("keydown", onKey);
       document.addEventListener("pointerdown", onPress);
       return () => {
         document.removeEventListener("keydown", onKey);
         document.removeEventListener("pointerdown", onPress);
       };
     }, [phase, close]);

     // Nothing held and nothing due (R1304002): nothing to show, as on `/collection`.
     if (quests !== null && quests.quests.length === 0 && quests.nextDueAt === null) return null;
     const held = quests?.quests.length ?? 0;
     const open = phase === "open";
     return (
       <div ref={root} className="landing-quests" style={{ "--quests-unroll": `${String(QUESTS_UNROLL_MS)}ms` } as CSSProperties}>
         <button
           ref={bookmark}
           type="button"
           className="landing-quests-bookmark"
           data-testid={landingTestid.questsBookmark}
           aria-label={t("Quests")}
           title={t("Quests")}
           aria-expanded={open}
           aria-controls={panelId}
           onClick={() => {
             if (open) close();
             else setPhase("open");
           }}
         >
           <QuestGlyph />
           {held > 0 ? (
             <span className="landing-quests-count" data-testid={landingTestid.questsCount} aria-hidden="true">
               {formatNumber(held)}
             </span>
           ) : null}
         </button>
         <div id={panelId} className="landing-quests-panel" data-testid={landingTestid.questsPanel} data-state={phase} data-motion={motion} hidden={phase === "closed"}>
           {phase === "closed" ? null : <QuestsView quests={quests} error={error} onRetry={reread} onArrived={reread} />}
         </div>
       </div>
     );
   }
   ```
   - `Actions({ questsToken, motion }: { questsToken: string | null; motion: LandingMotion })`: its last child, after the dev link, is `{questsToken === null ? null : <QuestsBookmark token={questsToken} motion={motion} />}`.
   - `LandingRouteProps` gets `/** R2035000: whether the economy is live, for the quests bookmark. */ economyLive?: boolean;`, defaulted in the signature `economyLive = ECONOMY_LIVE`.
   - After `useMotion()`, add `// R2035000: GET /api/quests answers an active account alone.` and `const questsToken = economyLive && account.kind === "ready" && account.me.profile.status === "active" ? account.token : null;`. Then render `<Actions questsToken={questsToken} motion={motion} />`.

